@startuml
' purpose: how `proveo run` finds a newer agent for the image it settled on, asks once, and reaches it without a source rebuild
' covers: internal/agentupdate/**
' covers: internal/imagebuild/overlay.go
' covers: internal/imagebuild/overlay_test.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/agent_update.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/provision.go (settleAgent, askAgentUpdate, attended)
' covers: internal/imagetest/overlay_test.go
' covers: internal/contract/agent_pin_test.go (overlay rows, TestEveryHarnessIsCoveredByTheAgentUpdateCheck)
' covers: internal/tmux/tmux.go (SessionEnv)
' covers: e2e/main_test.go
' covers: internal/envreg/envreg.go (PROVEO_AGENT_UPDATE)
'   the pin this check reads ........ _spec/_devops/agent-version-pin.puml
'   where the preflight sits ........ _spec/cmd/proveo/provision-and-targets.puml
'   the dialog it draws with ........ _spec/internal/choiceui/confirm-dialogs.puml
'   how FROM reaches sbx's kit build  _spec/internal/sbx/kit-image-source.puml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Agent update prompt — pull the published image, cover the gap with one layer, ask once per release
'
' ── THE DEFECT THIS CLOSES (MEASURED 2026-11-12) ───────────────────────────
' provisioner.Ensure pulls an image only when `docker image inspect` fails. A
' consumer who pulled proveo/claudecode:latest once kept that agent forever:
' on this host the local copy of the tag carried claude 2.1.312 (2026-10-29)
' while the registry copy, pushed the same day this was written, carried
' 2.1.322. `proveo update` replaces the CLI binary only. agent-version-pin.puml
' recorded the gap as STILL OPEN: the start line said WHICH release ran, never
' whether it was old.
' A local `:latest` is not the registry. `docker image inspect` reads the host
' store; `docker buildx imagetools inspect <ref> --format '{{json .Image}}'`
' reads the registry config (labels, created) without pulling a layer, 2.4 s.
'
' ── HOW sbx ANSWERS THE SAME QUESTION ──────────────────────────────────────
' sbx users never build. Since v0.51.0 (2026-11-03) a built-in agent name
' resolves to a published kit, docker.io/sbx/<name>, tagged by agent release;
' Docker rebuilds it as the agent ships (docker/sbx-releases#202, closed
' 2026-11-05). MEASURED from Docker Hub tags against npm publish times, four
' kits, 2.1.317 to 2.1.322: the kit trailed npm by 1.4 to 3.3 days, and
' 2.1.321 never got one. The gap is covered inside a long-lived sandbox by the
' agent's own updater (native installer under ~/.local, DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER
' unset, downloads.claude.ai allowed). sbx never prompts. Its stale-cache bug,
' #45, is this defect; its fix was to pull when the registry is newer.
'
' ── DECISIONS (the Executor, 2026-11-12) ───────────────────────────────────
' DELIVERY: "Pull + overlay for the gap". ANSWERS: "Update / Later 24h / Skip".
' Hermes resolves at build like the other defs (agent-version-pin.puml, HERMES).
' MEASURED before the choice, claudecode on this host:
'   pull after an agent-only bump   agent layer 162.5 MB compressed of 1106 MB;
'                                   every layer above it is under 0.1 MB
'   the same for claudecode-browser [Inference] about 380 MB: its 210.7 MB
'                                   browser layer sits above the agent layer
'   one-layer overlay               16.2 s, +507 MB without an npm cache mount
' NOT CHOSEN:
'   agent self-update, as sbx does  unpins the image; every agent's updater
'                                   differs; a session could plant a binary
'                                   on shared storage for later sandboxes
'   a host binary store, mounted ro most new proveo code; no hermes; exec over
'                                   virtiofs unmeasured
'   rebuild from source             a binary-only install has no defs/ tree,
'                                   and a cold cache rebuilds the whole chain
'   RUN lines in the kit recipe     sbx's kit build would redo the install
'                                   whenever BuildKit dropped the layer, so a
'                                   run that worked offline could need the
'                                   network at launch, with no question asked;
'                                   and the base image's label would name a
'                                   release the sandbox no longer runs
'
' ── WHAT COUNTS AS AN UPDATE ───────────────────────────────────────────────
' Settle(target, ref) runs after provisioner.Ensure, on every run that is not
' --print. It reads the image the run resolved (id, created, USER, the
' proveo.agent.version label), then decides from three facts:
'   carried    the release the run would launch: an overlay's when one is
'              built on this exact image id, else the image's own label
'   published  proveo.agent.version and `created` of PublishedRef(ref) in the
'              registry, for the host platform. :local and :latest both read
'              <repo>:latest; another tag reads itself; a digest pin is never
'              checked
'   upstream   Builder.Upstream(eco, pkg): the release source the build
'              resolves against, without the build's override or its printing
' PlanFor takes the shortest way to the newest release it can reach:
'   pull       published.created is after the local image's AND its agent is
'              newer. A republished image with the same agent is not an agent
'              update and is not offered; a local build newer than the
'              registry is never pulled over
'   overlay    upstream is newer than what the (pulled) image carries and the
'              pin has an Overlay recipe
'   behind     upstream is newer and the pin has none (hermes: the agent is
'              its upstream's whole image). One line per upstream release,
'              "<target> <v> is out — <repo> carries <v> until its image is
'              republished", and no offer
' Nothing is offered unless the plan's target is newer than carried.
' ORDER (imagebuild.Newer): the leading dotted number, numerically. Two
' releases with equal numbers and different text, or with no number, count as
' ahead: an offer the operator can Skip beats a release never mentioned. The
' github ecosystem compares by inequality alone, because upstream hermes left
' date tags (v2026.9.24) for v0.x and tag names stopped ordering.
'
' ── THE QUESTION ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   a newer claudecode agent is available
'   2.1.312 → 2.1.330
'
'   1. docker pull proveo/claudecode:latest (2.1.322)
'   2. install 2.1.330 on top as proveo/claudecode:agent-2.1.330
'
'   Later asks again in 24 hours.
'   Skip waits for a release after 2.1.330.
'    Later ↵    Update    Skip
' Later is the safe answer: Enter untouched, Esc and `n` give it, and it
' silences the check (no lookup, no question) for 24 hours. Skip records the
' plan's target; the next release asks again. Update runs the steps.
' WHO IS ASKED: only an attended run, by the predicate sandbox.headedConfirm
' already uses: PROVEO_SCHEDULE unset, the wizard on, stdin and stdout both
' terminals. A scheduled run sits in a tmux session and HAS a terminal, so a
' TTY test alone would park it on a dialog nobody sees.
' Unattended, or when /dev/tty will not open: one warning line, "<target> <a>
' → <b> is available — answer it in a terminal, or set PROVEO_AGENT_UPDATE=1
' to update without asking", and the run keeps its image.
' PROVEO_AGENT_UPDATE (envflag): ON updates without asking; OFF skips the
' check, yet an overlay already built is still launched.
'
' ── WHAT UPDATE DOES, AND WHAT IT LEAVES ───────────────────────────────────
' PULL: `docker pull <repo>:latest`. A run that resolved :local returns
' <repo>:latest afterwards, which maintain.ResolveImage also prefers from then
' on, since the pulled image is the newer one.
' OVERLAY: imagebuild.Overlay writes a four-instruction recipe to a temp dir:
'   FROM <base>  ·  USER root  ·  ARG <pin.Arg> (+ the spec's EnvArgs)
'   RUN <pin.Overlay>  ·  USER <the base's own USER>
'   LABEL proveo.agent.version=<v> proveo.agent.overlay.base=<base image id>
' and builds it `--load --pull=false` on HostBuilder (the buildx builder that
' reads the host store), tagged <repo>:agent-<version>. It exports no named
' cache. The recipe is the Dockerfile's own install step: agent_pin_test
' fails when a pin's Overlay stops matching its Dockerfile's install.
'   npm (claudecode, codex, opencode)  npm install -g <pkg>@<v> through a
'       cache mount, then the same --version check the Dockerfile makes.
'       opencode also rewrites /usr/local/lib/proveo/opencode.version and
'       refuses a major other than 2, as its Dockerfile does
'   cursor   re-runs the vendor installer, which installs whatever is current;
'       the recipe fails when that is no longer the release resolved
'   hermes   none
' THE OVERLAY IS AN IMAGE, NOT STATE. Each run lists <repo>:agent-* and uses
' the one whose overlay.base label equals the resolved image's id. An overlay
' of any other base is removed: a pull or a rebuild made it dead weight. A tag
' under agent-* without the label is not proveo's and is left alone. A new
' overlay is always built on the base, never on an overlay, so the image gains
' one layer however many releases pass; the superseded overlay is removed.
' A FAILED STEP NEVER FAILS THE RUN. A failed pull keeps the image already
' here; a failed install keeps the pulled image. Both warn with the error.
'
' ── HOW OFTEN THE NETWORK IS ASKED ─────────────────────────────────────────
' <state dir>/agent-update.json, one entry per image repo: checked, the
' published image's created and version, upstream, later, skip, noticed.
' One registry answer and one upstream answer serve 24 hours. Both lookups
' run at once, bounded at 6 s and 4 s. When neither answers the run stays
' silent and the next attempt waits one hour, not a day. An unreadable state
' file is an empty one.
'
' ── KNOWN LIMITS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   * The registry read needs the docker buildx plugin and the overlay needs a
'     docker-driver builder; without them the check stays silent and an
'     accepted overlay warns and keeps the image.
'   * `--print` skips the preflight, so it names the base image even when the
'     run would launch an overlay.
'   * An overlay launches an agent release nobody tested against that image's
'     entrypoint and seeds. The recipe's own --version check is the only gate.
'   * Freshness of the pull path is the maintainer's `mise run deploy`
'     cadence. [Inference] The 162.5 MB delta holds only while a publish
'     keeps the lower layers' digests; a cold builder republishes all of it.
'   * Tests: the e2e suite turns the check off (e2e/main_test.go sets
'     PROVEO_AGENT_UPDATE=0 and tmux.SessionEnv carries it into sessions,
'     which otherwise inherit the tmux server's environment). A test that
'     wants the dialog spells `env PROVEO_AGENT_UPDATE= proveo run …`.
'
' ── VERIFIED BY ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   internal/agentupdate/agentupdate_test.go   PlanFor table; Settle against a
'       fake store, registry and release source: pull, pull + overlay, overlay
'       reuse and replacement, stale and foreign tags, Later, Skip, the 24 h
'       cache, the 1 h offline retry, unattended, both switch values, failed
'       steps, :local → :latest, unreadable images, the hermes notice, a
'       corrupt state file, both docker documents
'   internal/imagebuild/overlay_test.go         Newer, AgentSpec, OverlayRef,
'       the recipe, the build argv, the two refusals
'   internal/choiceui/dialog_test.go            the copy, three answers, and
'       the rules every dialog obeys (safe first, two keys, 80 columns)
'   cmd/proveo/provision_test.go                attended, answer mapping
'   internal/imagetest/overlay_test.go (image)  each def's suite builds its
'       overlay for another real release over the real image and checks the
'       labels, USER, ENTRYPOINT and layer count

actor "Operator" as OP
participant "proveo run\npreflightImages" as PF <<app>>
participant "agentupdate.Checker\nSettle · PlanFor" as CHK <<app>>
database "agent-update.json\nstate dir" as ST <<db>>
participant "docker\nhost image store" as DK <<host>>
participant "registry\n<repo>:latest" as REG <<cloud>>
participant "agent release source\nnpm · cursor.com · GitHub" as UP <<cloud>>
participant "choiceui\nLater · Update · Skip" as DLG <<app>>
participant "imagebuild.Overlay\n<repo>:agent-<version>" as OV <<app>>

OP ARROW_MAIN PF : " ""proveo run <target>"" "
PF ARROW_MAIN DK : provisioner.Ensure — pull only when absent
PF ARROW_MAIN CHK : " ""Settle(target, ref)"" "
CHK ARROW_MAIN DK : inspect ref · list ""<repo>:agent-*""
DK ARROW_MAIN CHK : id · created · USER · version\n· the overlay built on this id, if any
CHK ARROW_MAIN ST : entry for the repo
alt later is in the future · or ""PROVEO_AGENT_UPDATE=0""
  CHK ARROW_OPTIONAL PF : the overlay, else ref — nothing asked
else checked over 24 h ago
  CHK ARROW_CLOUD REG : imagetools inspect (6 s)
  CHK ARROW_CLOUD UP : Builder.Upstream (4 s)
  REG ARROW_CLOUD CHK : created · proveo.agent.version
  UP ARROW_CLOUD CHK : current release
  CHK ARROW_MAIN ST : checked · published · upstream
else neither answered
  CHK ARROW_ERROR ST : retry in one hour — the run stays silent
end
CHK ARROW_MAIN CHK : PlanFor: pull? · overlay? · target
alt target is not newer than carried · or skipped
  CHK ARROW_OPTIONAL PF : the overlay, else ref
else unattended run
  CHK ARROW_OPTIONAL OP : one warning line, the run keeps its image
else attended
  CHK ARROW_MAIN DLG : from → to · the steps
  OP ARROW_MAIN DLG : Later (Enter, Esc) · Update · Skip
  DLG ARROW_MAIN CHK : the answer
  alt Update
    CHK ARROW_CLOUD REG : docker pull, when planned
    CHK ARROW_MAIN OV : install the release over the base
    OV ARROW_MAIN DK : one layer · two labels
    CHK ARROW_MAIN DK : remove the superseded overlay
    CHK ARROW_MAIN PF : the image to launch
  else Later
    CHK ARROW_MAIN ST : later = now + 24 h
  else Skip
    CHK ARROW_MAIN ST : skip = the plan's target
  end
end

note over DK
  A present image was never pulled again, so the
  first pull froze a consumer's agent. The check
  compares that image with its registry copy and
  with the agent's own release source.
end note

note over REG
  The registry answer is the image config alone:
  its labels and creation time, with no layer
  downloaded. One answer serves a full day, and
  an unreachable network leaves the run silent.
end note

note over OV
  The overlay installs one release over the base
  image in a single layer. A label names that
  base, so a pull or a rebuild retires the
  overlay instead of stacking another on it.
end note

note over DLG
  Later is the safe answer and quiets the check
  for a day. Skip waits for the next release.
  Only an attended run is asked: a scheduled
  run has a terminal and nobody watching it.
end note

note over UP
  An agent that is its upstream's whole image
  has no overlay. Its run names the release once
  and waits for the published image, which the
  pull step then delivers.
end note

@enduml
